# The mesh secret tree holds private keys AND the certs/CSRs issued alongside
# them at runtime — never commit its contents. Only the skeleton (.gitkeep)
# is tracked.
secrets/**
!secrets/
!secrets/**/
!secrets/**/.gitkeep

# Defence-in-depth: a PRIVATE key dropped anywhere under mesh/ (even outside
# secrets/) must never be committed. Public PKI material is intentionally NOT
# ignored here — *.crt certificates, *.csr signing requests, and *.pub keys are
# distributed by the PKI workflow and may be shared/tracked (README §2.3 "PKI
# pub", §3/§4 shared config+PKI on git). Runtime private material belongs in
# secrets/ (ignored wholesale above); these patterns only backstop mistakes.
*.key
*_key
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*.pfx
*.p12
*.p8
